TASK-202 runtime harness: Clear Cache & Redownload during the launch compile
from the cached list text, online and offline, with the lists served by a
URLProtocol (no network). Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Gated
on DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR.

    SP=<scratch>; mkdir -p $SP/served $SP/out
    # served/<id>.txt: the four filter lists (copies of 2026-10-26) with three
    # extra rules appended (||t202-redownload-{a,b,c}.example^), so the
    # redownload's counts (71,319 / 56,313 / 25,082 / 102,778) differ from
    # the cached text's (71,316 / 56,310 / 25,079 / 102,775).
    git apply docs/harness/task202-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # run.sh <run> <data dir> <offline 0|1>: seeds a FRESH
    # ~/Library/Application Support/<data dir>/ContentBlocker/<id>.txt with
    # the unmodified copies (the "cached text"), streams the build's
    # content-blocker os_log (log stream, processImagePath CONTAINS
    # ".derived"), launches
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=<data dir> DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_RUN=<run> \
        DETOUR_VERIFY_LISTS=$SP/served DETOUR_VERIFY_OFFLINE=<0|1> \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # serves SHOOT lines with screencapture -l, kills only that PID after "done"
    git apply -R docs/harness/task202-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

The harness keeps AppDelegate from starting the content blocker. After 12 s
of HID idle it opens Settings > Content Blocking, calls
ContentBlockerManager.initialize() (nothing compiled, so every list compiles
from its cached text, the launch path), waits until easylist's compile has
been handed to the store (its ruleCount key is written on main just before),
waits 1.5 s and clicks "Clear Cache & Redownload": a posted click, and when
that does not land within 1 s (a locked screen drops posted events) the
button's performClick. It logs each list's rulesFormat, In List, Active,
chunks, refreshing state, cache text, ETag and lastFetch before, at and right
after the click, then once nothing has changed for 20 s, with the rule list
store's files and the Settings pane's texts.

Results (2026-10-27):
- "offline" (DetourVerify2021, posted click; the screen locked after this
  run, so the later runs used performClick): os_log "Not compiling
